# Prestium 1.9.1 Tor configuration (on top of /usr/share/tor/tor-service-defaults-torrc)
#
# A SocksPort line here replaces every SocksPort of the defaults file, so the
# world-writable unix socket /run/tor/socks (which the per-uid firewall can't
# filter) is gone. Streams to different destination hosts/ports use separate
# circuits; Tor Browser isolates further by SOCKS username (first-party domain).
SocksPort 127.0.0.1:9050 IsolateDestAddr IsolateDestPort
# no DNSPort/TransPort: nothing on Prestium resolves names outside Tor/I2P
AvoidDiskWrites 1
# Sandbox 1 removed in 1.9.1: Tor refuses managed proxies (ClientTransportPlugin: obfs4/snowflake/webtunnel) in Sandbox mode, so tor@default failed. Tails does not use Sandbox either.
# IPv6 is disabled on Prestium
ClientUseIPv6 0
ClientPreferIPv6ORPort 0

# Pluggable transports: obfs4 (lyrebird), Snowflake and WebTunnel are set up by the Tor Connection
# Assistant (menu: Network). Snowflake/meek/WebTunnel host names are resolved with DNS-over-HTTPS
# through the I2P outproxy and pinned for the transports; Tor traffic itself never uses I2P.

# Prestium 2.0: pluggable transports, bridges and UseBridges live in the Tor Connection
# Assistant's drop-in (/etc/tor/torrc.d/50-prestium-assistant.conf; default = direct connection).
%include /etc/tor/torrc.d/*.conf
